Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Sepulchral Primordial: "When this creature enters, for each opponent, you
may put up to one target creature card from that player's graveyard onto
the battlefield under your control."

CR 115.1 + CR 601.2c: the trigger has up to one target per opponent,
each from that opponent's graveyard. phase parsed one target in all (and
the swallow check flagged the lost iteration). The sentence now reads as
"you may put any number of target creature cards from an opponent's
graveyard controlled by different players onto the battlefield under
your control", the grammar Windgrace's Judgment uses: an unbounded
multi-target with TargetSelectionConstraint::DifferentObjectControllers.
CR 108.4a: a card in a graveyard is controlled by its owner, so no two
targets come from the same graveyard. The swallow check counts that form
as the per-opponent iteration. Only the "put" instruction is rewritten;
a per-opponent free cast keeps its paired fan-out.

Card data: the parse change reaches games only with card data generated
by this parser.

Test: tests/integration/sepulchral_primordial_one_per_graveyard.rs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
